# halfcenter v57c -- the WINNER SETTLES, which is the theory's own prediction.
# 2026-09-18. Gated on verify PASS (hash ad96f882becbee92, 22 experiments, 7.6 min).
#
# The kill switch passed every arm this time: duty 0.29-0.57, rate 1.82-2.46
# against a 4.93 baseline, no runaway and no silence. So the mechanism is stable.
#
# BUT ANTI-PHASE READ EXACTLY +/-0.000 IN EVERY hc>0 ARM, WITH SE EXACTLY 0.000
# ACROSS TWELVE SEEDS. An SE of exactly zero is impossible for a real
# correlation. It was hc_corr() returning its degenerate guard (cxx <= 0, i.e.
# one series CONSTANT) and the caller printing that as 'no anti-phase'.
#
# THE DIAGNOSIS, from a quantity already in the table: half-diff SNR is 4.2-4.7,
# NOT zero. The half-DIFFERENCE varies while the correlation guard fires, which
# means ONE half of the F1 group is silenced and the other is not. That is a
# permanent WINNER-TAKE-ALL -- and Matsuoka 1985 is precisely that mutual
# inhibition ALONE settles into a winner, with adaptation the thing that
# releases it. At adapt_jump 0.05 against hc 0.60-3.00 the fatigue is 12-60x
# weaker than the inhibition, so it cannot release anything.
#
# SO THIS IS NOT A REFUSAL OF THE HALF-CENTER. It is the half-center doing
# exactly what half a half-center must do. The printed verdict is RETRACTED for
# the third time.
#
# WHY THE FATIGUE COULD NOT BE RAISED, and the fix. Adaptation was MODULE-WIDE
# while the competition sits in group 2, so raising adapt_jump enough to release
# the winner also hit the voicing gate (group 1) and amplitude (group 8) and
# muted the voice -- adaptclock measured duty 0.01 at jump 0.15. v57c scopes the
# adaptation to the competing populations when a half-center is running. Checked
# at 1.2M ticks: adapt_jump 1.00 (20x the value that muted the larynx) now gives
# rate 4.00 Hz, duty 0.51, babble PASS. halfcenter_gain ships at 0 so nothing
# retroactively changes -- adaptclock ran hc off and is untouched.
